  "slug": "untitled-topic-b83f",
  "summary": "Four 2026 preprints add agentic, database, web-based and nanopore tools for microbiome sequence and proteomic analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is tool-level development for microbial sequence and proteomic analysis, with emphasis on automation, reference resources and accessible deployment. MicroBioAgent proposes an autonomous AI agent that builds and runs adaptive pipelines for 16S, shotgun and de novo metagenomic analysis. RADSuite pairs RADlib, a curated 16S rRNA gene copy database, with RADx, which identifies V regions to enable species-level microbiome identification. Unipept's 2026 update moves multi-sample metaproteomics, including project organization, comparison and pathway mapping, into a web platform. ONTOLOGY offers a GUI-driven workflow with freeze-dried PCR plates and two pipelines for nanopore DNA barcoding and metabarcoding, aimed at decentralized use. Together these preprints address workflow design, taxonomic resolution and usability rather than reporting new biological findings. The novelty lies in combining curated reference data, agent-based automation and point-of-use access within analysis pipelines.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
